        "United Muslim Relief demonstrates strong organizational governance and outreach scale. It holds an <cite id=\"1\">overall rating of 94.5/100 from Charity Navigator</cite>, supported by a high leadership score [1]. Operational delivery is backed by extensive partnerships, allowing the organization to serve millions across multiple crisis zones [4]. Financial stewardship is reinforced by meeting <cite id=\"1\">all 20 BBB Wise Giving Alliance Standards</cite> [1]."
      ],
      "summary": "United Muslim Relief operates as a major humanitarian provider delivering global health, water access, and emergency relief [4]. Founded in 2014 [1], the organization generated <cite id=\"3\">$149,888,609 in total revenue in FY2024</cite> with a <cite id=\"3\">3-year revenue CAGR of 191.2%</cite>. UMR manages extensive international programming across regions like Sudan, Yemen, and Bangladesh [4]. It holds an <cite id=\"1\">overall rating of 94.5/100 from Charity Navigator</cite> and meets all <cite id=\"1\">20 BBB Wise Giving Alliance Standards</cite> [1]. UMR provides verified <cite id=\"2\">zakat-eligible assistance</cite> to support vulnerable populations [2]. While its reported Form 990 filing indicates a <cite id=\"3\">47.5% program expense Ratio in FY2024</cite>, its cash-adjusted program ratio drops to 48% when excluding non-cash donations [3]. UMR maintains lean operations with a low <cite id=\"1\">fundraising efficiency of $0.05 per $1 raised</cite> [1]. However, it faces financial continuity risks due to having only 0.2 to 0.3 months of working capital reserves [1].",
